1
00:00:03,849 --> 00:00:06,278
The Lives of the Prophets Part 1;

2
00:00:06,778 --> 00:00:10,492
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,634
And then he told his son;

4
00:00:12,927 --> 00:00:43,483
وَكَذٰلِكَ يَجتَبيكَ رَبُّكَ وَيُعَلِّمُكَ مِن تَأويلِ الأَحاديثِ وَيُتِمُّ نِعمَتَهُ عَلَيكَ وَعَلىٰ آلِ يَعقوبَ

5
00:00:48,914 --> 00:01:21,819
وَيُتِمُّ نِعمَتَهُ عَلَيكَ وَعَلىٰ آلِ يَعقوبَ كَما أَتَمَّها عَلىٰ أَبَوَيكَ مِن قَبلُ إِبراهيمَ وَإِسحاقَ ۚ

6
00:01:24,422 --> 00:01:34,046
إِنَّ رَبَّكَ عَليمٌ حَكيمٌ۝

7
00:01:34,536 --> 00:01:38,331
And all of these things he's deriving from this dream.

8
00:01:38,578 --> 00:01:40,764
Thus will your Lord choose you,

9
00:01:41,486 --> 00:01:47,375
Allah will choose you and teach you the interpretation of dreams and other things.

10
00:01:47,642 --> 00:01:48,907
Taweel Al- Ahadith(تَأويل احاديث);

11
00:01:49,385 --> 00:01:50,635
Taweel(تأويل) is interpretation,

12
00:01:50,665 --> 00:01:54,599
Ahadith(احاديث) are speeches, words, dreams, different things.

13
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:57,573
So it doesn't necessarily mean only dreams.

14
00:01:57,899 --> 00:02:04,539
It means that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will give you wisdom to interpret things to have a good judgment

15
00:02:04,822 --> 00:02:09,912
and He will perfect his favor on you and on the offspring of Yaqoob(يعقوب)

16
00:02:09,942 --> 00:02:13,976
as he perfected it on your father's Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Is'haq(إسحاق) afore time.

17
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,365
Verily your Lord is all Knowing all Wise.

18
00:02:17,143 --> 00:02:20,357
Some men came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and they told him;

19
00:02:20,387 --> 00:02:21,523
  من أكرم الناس

20
00:02:21,619 --> 00:02:24,849
Who is the most noble of men.

21
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,080
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

22
00:02:28,734 --> 00:02:33,750
يوسُف الْكَرِيمُ ابنُ الكَرِيمِ ابْنِ الكَرِيمِ ابْنِ الكَرِيمِ

23
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:39,318
It is Yusuf(يوسُف) the Noble, the son of the Noble, the son of the Noble, the son of the Noble.

24
00:02:39,695 --> 00:02:45,977
If you're asking me about the best lineage, it is Yusuf(يوسُف) the father of Yusuf(يوسُف) is a prophet.

25
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:50,782
His grandfather is a Prophet and his great grandfather is a prophet and he is a prophet himself.

26
00:02:50,905 --> 00:02:53,756
That's the best lineage if you want to look at it this way,

27
00:02:53,979 --> 00:02:57,439
يُوسُفُ إبنُ يَعْقُوبَ إبنِ إسْحاقَ إبنِ إبْراهِيمَ، عليهمُ السَّلاَمُ

28
00:02:58,844 --> 00:03:02,436
It's an honor from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to be a prophet

29
00:03:02,466 --> 00:03:06,811
and your father is a prophet and your grandfather is a prophet and your great grandfather is a prophet.

30
00:03:07,056 --> 00:03:11,507
Wherever you look up, you find the guidance of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, an honor from Allah.

31
00:03:12,895 --> 00:03:14,816
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling us.

32
00:03:14,959 --> 00:03:32,647
لَقَد كانَ في يوسُفَ وَإِخوَتِهِ آياتٌ لِلسّائِلينَ۝

33
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:38,334
Verily in Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brethren, there were for Ayaat(آيات) for those, who ask.

34
00:03:39,611 --> 00:03:42,576
If you look at the story of Yusuf(يوسُف) and you think about it,

35
00:03:42,965 --> 00:03:50,198
you would find in it, an ocean of meanings and lessons that will assist you in your life.

36
00:03:53,023 --> 00:03:57,419
The brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) knew that their father loved him more than them.

37
00:03:57,687 --> 00:04:02,772
10 of them were from Different mother or mothers,

38
00:04:03,177 --> 00:04:08,241
and Yusuf(يوسُف) and Binyamin(بنيامين) were from another wife of Sayedina Yaqoob(سيدنا يعقوب).

39
00:04:08,852 --> 00:04:13,045
Yusuf(يوسُف) was the most beloved in the eyes of his father.

40
00:04:14,274 --> 00:04:17,999
And these brothers dislike that, and they were jealous.

41
00:04:18,355 --> 00:04:20,752
And we said that jealousy blinds the heart.

42
00:04:21,363 --> 00:04:22,026
They said;

43
00:04:22,056 --> 00:04:32,748
إِنَّ أَبانا لَفي ضَلالٍ مُبينٍ۝

44
00:04:32,835 --> 00:04:33,279
They said;

45
00:04:33,309 --> 00:04:35,206
Our Father is in plain error.

46
00:04:35,264 --> 00:04:36,067
 Why?

47
00:04:36,219 --> 00:04:38,283
Because he loves Yusuf(يوسُف) more than us.

48
00:04:38,674 --> 00:04:43,045
We are the men, we are the elders, we are the strongest, we are a group,

49
00:04:43,473 --> 00:04:46,360
we are the ones who are going to help our Father in moments of need.

50
00:04:46,891 --> 00:04:53,513
How can he love this Yusuf(يوسُف) and his brother who are young and alone.

51
00:04:53,795 --> 00:04:58,166
I mean in those times, what protects you is your family

52
00:04:59,563 --> 00:05:05,456
They didn't have laws and laws and law enforcement and police to take care of security.

53
00:05:05,995 --> 00:05:08,646
You protect yourself through your family.

54
00:05:09,154 --> 00:05:13,805
And that's why they used to be proud whenever they have a lot of family members,

55
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:16,630
the bigger your family member, the stronger you become.

56
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:17,504
So they said;

57
00:05:17,534 --> 00:05:18,459
وَنَحنُ عُصبَةٌ

58
00:05:18,682 --> 00:05:20,508
We are the men, who are strong.

59
00:05:20,722 --> 00:05:26,435
How can our father love Yusuf(يوسُف) more than us and then they accuse their father of being an error, Zallal(ضَلالٍ) misguided.

60
00:05:26,641 --> 00:05:29,776
And this is not the right thing to say about your father that your father misguided,

61
00:05:30,054 --> 00:05:34,057
and you know that your father is a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, this is because of jealousy.

62
00:05:34,311 --> 00:05:41,024
The brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) made a plan to kill, assassinate their brother.

63
00:05:42,469 --> 00:05:47,119
Look at how jealousy made their thinking crooked.

64
00:05:47,984 --> 00:05:55,174
The small issue of the love of their father to Yusuf(يوسُف), became very big in their eyes.

65
00:05:56,174 --> 00:06:01,194
And the big issue of killing a human soul became very smell and insignificant.

66
00:06:02,807 --> 00:06:04,383
It's all because of jealousy.

67
00:06:04,923 --> 00:06:11,441
So jealousy made them see this little more love that Yaqoob(يعقوب) has to a son;

68
00:06:11,703 --> 00:06:13,544
It's just a little much more love,

69
00:06:13,734 --> 00:06:15,871
because he loves them all, all of them are his children,

70
00:06:16,132 --> 00:06:19,482
but just because he loves Yusuf(يوسُف) of a little bit more.

71
00:06:19,618 --> 00:06:26,610
They saw that as a great deal, a big thing, and it obsessed them and overwhelmed them and overtook their thinking,

72
00:06:26,927 --> 00:06:30,918
but then killing a human being, is something normal and small.

73
00:06:31,784 --> 00:06:32,228
Why?

74
00:06:32,258 --> 00:06:33,188
Because of jealousy.

75
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:34,574
  اقتُلوا يوسُفَ

76
00:06:34,634 --> 00:06:35,274
kill him.

77
00:06:35,712 --> 00:06:37,540
  أَوِ اطرَحوهُ أَرضًا

78
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:41,049
or throw him out in a foreign land?

79
00:06:41,366 --> 00:06:45,964
يَخلُ لَكُم وَجهُ أَبيكُم وَتَكونوا مِن بَعدِهِ قَومًا صالِحينَ۝

80
00:06:46,274 --> 00:06:52,393
Your father would give you the favors alone, and after that you would be righteous folks.

81
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:55,627
They intended to make At-Toba(التوبة) before making the sin.

82
00:06:56,150 --> 00:06:58,418
They said: We're going to kill him and then we're going to make At-Toba(التوبة).

83
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:02,250
One of them; who was the softest among them.

84
00:07:02,691 --> 00:07:07,310
He said; No! Don't kill Yusuf(يوسُف); Instead, throw him in the well.

85
00:07:07,858 --> 00:07:40,376
قالَ قائِلٌ مِنهُم لا تَقتُلوا يوسُفَ وَأَلقوهُ في غَيابَتِ الجُبِّ يَلتَقِطهُ بَعضُ السَّيّارَةِ إِن كُنتُم فاعِلينَ۝

86
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:46,965
One of them said: Kill not Yusuf(يوسُف) but if you must do something, throw him down to the bottom of a well,

87
00:07:47,155 --> 00:07:50,139
 he will be picked up by some caravan of travelers.

88
00:07:50,624 --> 00:07:53,127
So they made a deal that they're gonna throw him in a well.

89
00:07:54,353 --> 00:07:57,860
And then whenever somebody would come and take water from that well,

90
00:07:57,976 --> 00:08:00,712
they're going to pick up Yusuf(يوسُف) and they're going to carry him with them

91
00:08:00,742 --> 00:08:03,537
and we're going to get rid of him that way, let's not kill him.

92
00:08:04,124 --> 00:08:05,344
So they went to the Father.

93
00:08:05,566 --> 00:08:13,383
And they said: O our Father, why don't you trust us with yusuf(يوسف) we're strong men, we'll take care of him.

94
00:08:13,486 --> 00:08:15,177
Let him come out and play with us.

95
00:08:16,351 --> 00:08:20,743
Yaqoob(يعقوب) was so protective of his son, he would not let them go out and play with them.

96
00:08:21,916 --> 00:08:24,979
He is always with him, he used to love his son so much.

97
00:08:25,988 --> 00:08:26,805
They said;

98
00:08:27,074 --> 00:08:50,626
قالوا يا أَبانا ما لَكَ لا تَأمَنّا عَلىٰ يوسُفَ وَإِنّا لَهُ لَناصِحونَ۝

99
00:08:51,111 --> 00:08:58,228
Oh Our Father, why you not trust us with Yusuf(يوسُف), when we are indeed his well wishers.

100
00:08:58,730 --> 00:09:03,063
Send him with us tomorrow, to enjoy himself and play, verily will take care of him.

101
00:09:03,452 --> 00:09:05,646
قالَ إِنّي لَيَحزُنُني أَن تَذهَبوا بِهِ

102
00:09:05,797 --> 00:09:06,599
He said;

103
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:10,416
Truly it saddens me that you should take him away from me.

104
00:09:10,726 --> 00:09:15,913
Yaqoob عليه السّلام loves his son so much he can't even stand letting his son go out for a day.

105
00:09:17,064 --> 00:09:21,411
I would feel sorrow, I would feel sad if you take away Yusuf(يوسُف) it from me.

106
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:23,164
He used to love his son so much.

107
00:09:23,846 --> 00:09:27,584
One day is too much for him. He can't let go of his son for a day.

108
00:09:28,012 --> 00:09:29,115
And then he said;

109
00:09:29,909 --> 00:09:33,425
وَأَخافُ أَن يَأكُلَهُ الذِّئبُ وَأَنتُم عَنهُ غافِلونَ۝

110
00:09:33,455 --> 00:09:38,014
I fear lest, a wolf should devour him while you are careless of him.

111
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:44,079
So they picked up this from their father and then they use it.

112
00:09:45,015 --> 00:09:48,634
The father said I'm worried that a wolf would kill him.

113
00:09:49,395 --> 00:09:52,390
These brothers were so much in a hurry to get rid of Yusuf(يوسُف)

114
00:09:52,564 --> 00:09:54,945
they didn't even have time to perfect their plan.

115
00:09:55,056 --> 00:09:57,191
So they picked up this word of their father.

116
00:09:57,429 --> 00:09:59,922
They took out Yusuf(يوسُف) to go out and play.

117
00:10:00,305 --> 00:10:01,815
They threw him in a well,

118
00:10:02,386 --> 00:10:10,217
and then they took his clothes and they slaughtered the small goat and they poured the blood of that goat on his clothes.

119
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:13,663
And then they went back to their father crying.

120
00:10:14,432 --> 00:10:16,544
And they said: Our father the wolf ate him.

121
00:10:18,051 --> 00:10:21,500
He told him I'm afraid that the wolf the wolf ate him they said OK let's say that wolf ate him.

122
00:10:22,127 --> 00:10:23,372
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

123
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:39,684
فَلَمّا ذَهَبوا بِهِ وَأَجمَعوا أَن يَجعَلوهُ في غَيابَتِ الجُبِّ ۚ

124
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:45,805
So when they took him away, they all agreed to throw him down to the bottom of the well.

125
00:10:47,067 --> 00:10:52,409
When they were throwing him in the well, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى reveal to Yusuf(يوسُف).

126
00:10:52,599 --> 00:11:13,816
وَأَوحَينا إِلَيهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُم بِأَمرِهِم هٰذا وَهُم لا يَشعُرونَ۝

127
00:11:14,248 --> 00:11:16,468
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى revealed to Yusuf(يوسُف)

128
00:11:16,992 --> 00:11:25,080
and we inspire in him, indeed you shall one day inform them of this affair while they know you not.

129
00:11:26,088 --> 00:11:27,963
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Yusuf(يوسُف);

130
00:11:28,487 --> 00:11:36,440
One day you will tell your brothers about this event and they would not know that it is you, who's speaking to them.

131
00:11:38,432 --> 00:11:44,024
Allah is telling Yusuf(يوسُف) about something but Yusuf(يوسُف) does not know the details of it,

132
00:11:44,278 --> 00:11:49,429
when it will happen, it's a prophecy that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has inspired to SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

133
00:11:50,199 --> 00:12:04,805
وَجاءوا أَباهُم عِشاءً يَبكونَ۝

134
00:12:05,032 --> 00:12:11,057
And they came to their fathers in the early part of the night weeping, they were crying.

135
00:12:11,422 --> 00:12:50,620
قالوا يا أَبانا إِنّا ذَهَبنا نَستَبِقُ وَتَرَكنا يوسُفَ عِندَ مَتاعِنا فَأَكَلَهُ الذِّئبُ ۖ وَما أَنتَ بِمُؤمِنٍ لَنا وَلَو كُنّا صادِقينَ۝

136
00:12:51,203 --> 00:12:54,242
They said: O our Father we went racing with one another

137
00:12:54,480 --> 00:13:00,162
and left Yusuf(يوسُف) by our belongings and wolf devoured him, but you will never believe us.

138
00:13:00,192 --> 00:13:02,313
Even when we speak the truth.

139
00:13:02,877 --> 00:13:09,152
Once one of the Muslim judges, an old woman came to him in a case

140
00:13:11,271 --> 00:13:15,025
and she was crying so much crying and crying, crying.

141
00:13:15,938 --> 00:13:17,720
The judge ruled against her.

142
00:13:18,450 --> 00:13:20,029
So then the friend of the judge said;

143
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:22,696
She's crying so much she must be telling the truth.

144
00:13:22,807 --> 00:13:23,950
Why didn't you believe her?

145
00:13:24,283 --> 00:13:28,573
He said, didn't you read the Qur'an that the brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) came to their father at night crying?

146
00:13:29,422 --> 00:13:34,349
Crying is not a sign of innocence, crying is not a sign of truth.

147
00:13:34,811 --> 00:13:37,136
You could cry while you're lying.

148
00:13:37,668 --> 00:13:42,782
So over here, the brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف), they came back home crying, but they are the ones who committed the crime.

149
00:13:43,814 --> 00:13:45,284
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

150
00:13:46,006 --> 00:13:57,004
وَجاءوا عَلىٰ قَميصِهِ بِدَمٍ كَذِبٍ ۚ

151
00:13:59,551 --> 00:14:16,611
قالَ بَل سَوَّلَت لَكُم أَنفُسُكُم أَمرًا ۖ فَصَبرٌ جَميلٌ ۖ

152
00:14:18,544 --> 00:14:29,813
وَاللَّهُ المُستَعانُ عَلىٰ ما تَصِفونَ۝

153
00:14:30,155 --> 00:14:32,908
And they brought his shirt stained with false blood.

154
00:14:33,067 --> 00:14:34,958
He said, this is Yaqoob(يعقوب);

155
00:14:35,029 --> 00:14:38,926
Nay! But your own selves have made up a tale.

156
00:14:39,529 --> 00:14:40,902
He knew that they're lying.

157
00:14:41,116 --> 00:14:48,068
So patience is most fitting, and it is Allah alone, whose help can be sought against that which you assert.

158
00:14:48,155 --> 00:14:50,671
I mean, what is he going to do, is he going to kill his sons?

159
00:14:52,093 --> 00:14:53,697
This is a dilemma for the Father.

160
00:14:54,403 --> 00:14:55,736
Is he going to kill his sons?

161
00:14:56,204 --> 00:14:56,609
So he said;

162
00:14:56,669 --> 00:14:57,503
  صبرٌ جميل

163
00:14:57,712 --> 00:14:58,878
I will have patience

164
00:14:59,133 --> 00:15:00,241
 الله المستعان

165
00:15:00,368 --> 00:15:02,749
and I would seek assistance from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى .

166
00:15:06,281 --> 00:15:07,642
Yusuf(يوسُف) was in well.

167
00:15:08,714 --> 00:15:10,797
A caravan of travelers pass by;

168
00:15:11,709 --> 00:15:12,772
  فَاَرسِلو واردهم

169
00:15:12,802 --> 00:15:15,067
they sent somebody to go and get water for them.

170
00:15:16,281 --> 00:15:25,167
So he inserted the bucket in the well and Yusuf(يوسُف) cling to the bucket.

171
00:15:25,789 --> 00:15:30,725
And this man is pulling up the bucket looking forward to get some water, he finds in there a child.

172
00:15:31,432 --> 00:15:31,725
He said;

173
00:15:31,755 --> 00:15:33,303
يا بُشرىٰ هٰذا غُلامٌ

174
00:15:33,363 --> 00:15:34,655
He was so happy.

175
00:15:35,275 --> 00:15:35,687
Why?

176
00:15:35,717 --> 00:15:38,068
Because this is a fortune.

177
00:15:39,196 --> 00:15:44,072
In those times, slaves would get you a lot of money.

178
00:15:44,842 --> 00:15:50,493
So they felt that they are going to sell this young child and it's a very good deal for them.

179
00:15:51,109 --> 00:15:59,365
So they picked him up, took him with them in their caravan, and they went to Egypt and they sold him in Egypt.

180
00:16:00,270 --> 00:16:01,656
They Sold him for a good price.

181
00:16:01,898 --> 00:16:03,466
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

182
00:16:03,541 --> 00:16:25,156
وَشَرَوهُ بِثَمَنٍ بَخسٍ دَراهِمَ مَعدودَةٍ وَكانوا فيهِ مِنَ الزّاهِدينَ۝

183
00:16:25,603 --> 00:16:28,037
And they sold them for a low price.

184
00:16:28,196 --> 00:16:28,952
Why?

185
00:16:30,471 --> 00:16:32,566
Even though they got a good deal for Yusuf(يوسُف),

186
00:16:32,979 --> 00:16:38,066
but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saying it's a low price because they never knew, who was in their hands.

187
00:16:39,137 --> 00:16:41,336
They don't know who is the one they sold.

188
00:16:41,947 --> 00:16:45,161
They don't know who this who this child will grow up to be.

189
00:16:46,381 --> 00:16:52,691
And if they would have sold him with his weight in gold, that would have been a cheap price.

190
00:16:55,404 --> 00:16:56,706
وَكانوا فيهِ مِنَ الزّاهِدينَ۝

191
00:16:56,730 --> 00:17:00,095
And they were of those who regarded him as insignificant.

192
00:17:00,349 --> 00:17:04,057
They didn’t know who he was this is Ghaib(غيب) in the eyes of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, unseen.

193
00:17:04,793 --> 00:17:33,975
وَقالَ الَّذِي اشتَراهُ مِن مِصرَ لِامرَأَتِهِ أَكرِمي مَثواهُ عَسىٰ أَن يَنفَعَنا أَو نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا ۚ

194
00:17:34,205 --> 00:17:38,353
And he, the man from Egypt who bought him said to his wife;

195
00:17:38,631 --> 00:17:45,483
Make his stay comfortable, maybe he will profit us or we shall adopt him as a son.

196
00:17:46,045 --> 00:17:49,458
One of the Salaf(سلف), he says;

197
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:56,854
Three persons had a very, very good Farasah(فراسة).

198
00:17:57,433 --> 00:18:01,958
Farasah(فراسة) is the ability to foresee an event, or to look in the future.

199
00:18:03,328 --> 00:18:08,020
He said; One of them is this man in Egypt, he bought Yusuf(يوسُف)

200
00:18:08,645 --> 00:18:13,411
and he said maybe one day he will benefit us, maybe this man will have a future.

201
00:18:14,794 --> 00:18:16,470
The second is;

202
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:21,626
The daughter of the man in Madyan(مَدْيَن) who went to her father and said;

203
00:18:21,753 --> 00:18:24,817
ٱسْتَـْٔجِرْهُ ۖ إِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ ٱسْتَـْٔجَرْتَ ٱلْقَوِىُّ ٱلْأَمِينُ

204
00:18:25,246 --> 00:18:29,637
Hire him to work for you because the best man you could hire is a strong and trustworthy,

205
00:18:29,812 --> 00:18:31,026
she was speaking about who?

206
00:18:31,383 --> 00:18:32,193
Musa(موسى).

207
00:18:33,375 --> 00:18:35,094
And third one is

208
00:18:35,117 --> 00:18:38,872
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), when he appointed me Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to be the Khalifah(خليفه).

209
00:18:40,459 --> 00:18:44,832
He said: These are three man who had the best Farasah(فراسة), best vision ahead.

210
00:18:45,788 --> 00:19:06,116
وَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنّا لِيوسُفَ فِي الأَرضِ وَلِنُعَلِّمَهُ مِن تَأويلِ الأَحاديثِ ۚ

211
00:19:06,614 --> 00:19:12,789
Thus did we established Yusuf(يوسُف) in the land, that we might teach him the interpretation of events.

212
00:19:13,075 --> 00:19:20,996
Yusuf عليه السّلام, went through slavery and was bought and sold and went through this difficulty in his life.

213
00:19:21,313 --> 00:19:21,609
Why?

214
00:19:21,639 --> 00:19:24,544
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to establish him on Earth.

215
00:19:26,536 --> 00:19:27,382
 Lit-Tamkeen(لأتمكين)

216
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:31,399
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is putting this Ummah(امة) in difficulty.

217
00:19:31,429 --> 00:19:32,221
Why?

218
00:19:33,224 --> 00:19:37,115
To prepare them for their establishment in the land.

219
00:19:37,821 --> 00:19:41,162
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put the Sahabah(صحابه) and Rasool Allah ﷺ in difficulty.

220
00:19:41,192 --> 00:19:42,078
Why?

221
00:19:42,543 --> 00:19:46,749
So that one day they will be prepared and ready for the establishment on the land.

222
00:19:47,178 --> 00:19:50,591
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put Musa(موسى) through misery and difficulty

223
00:19:50,621 --> 00:19:53,459
and we're going to talk about the amazing story of Musa(موسى),

224
00:19:53,752 --> 00:19:57,525
the difficulty that he went through and the struggling and the striving,

225
00:19:57,555 --> 00:19:58,128
why?

226
00:19:58,319 --> 00:20:00,422
So that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will establish him.

227
00:20:01,089 --> 00:20:02,517
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

228
00:20:03,303 --> 00:20:06,286
وَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنّا لِيوسُفَ فِي الأَرضِ

229
00:20:06,784 --> 00:20:08,302
Thus did we establish

230
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:10,691
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is calling this, establishment

231
00:20:11,032 --> 00:20:16,515
because he got to Egypt, even though he was a slave, but that was the establishment for him in the future.

232
00:20:16,856 --> 00:20:18,544
وَلِنُعَلِّمَهُ مِن تَأويلِ الأَحاديثِ ۚ

233
00:20:18,568 --> 00:20:21,341
And we teach him the interpretation of events,

234
00:20:21,658 --> 00:20:27,251
Yusuf(يوسُف) is living through a life experience so that he would develop knowledge and experience.

235
00:20:28,307 --> 00:20:29,720
He's going through a lot.

236
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:35,148
And notice that Yusuf عليه السّلام, where is he being trained now.

237
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:38,610
He's been trained in the house of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز).

238
00:20:39,285 --> 00:20:43,751
Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) is like the prime minister in modern terms,

239
00:20:44,172 --> 00:20:50,251
not only the Prime Minister, but it's even stronger than that because he's also the treasurer in the same time,

240
00:20:50,577 --> 00:20:53,394
the second most important post after the king.

241
00:20:53,943 --> 00:20:57,632
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put Yusuf(يوسُف) in that environment even though he's a slave.

242
00:20:57,870 --> 00:21:00,998
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is putting him in the decision making Center.

243
00:21:01,744 --> 00:21:04,990
He is close to these events to learn, to gain experience.

244
00:21:05,744 --> 00:21:08,184
Just like Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has put Musa(موسى) where?

245
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:10,026
In the house of Firaun(فرعون).

246
00:21:10,994 --> 00:21:12,734
وَاللَّهُ غالِبٌ عَلىٰ أَمرِهِ

247
00:21:12,903 --> 00:21:16,550
And Allah has full power and control over His affairs.

248
00:21:16,939 --> 00:21:20,708
The brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف) thought that they have control over affairs and they're going to get rid of him.

249
00:21:21,351 --> 00:21:25,848
But as soon as they put Yusuf(يوسُف) in the well the matter is out of their hands.

250
00:21:26,150 --> 00:21:31,118
Now Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is taking care of Yusuf(يوسُف) and things are going to turn around against them.

251
00:21:31,411 --> 00:21:33,338
وَلٰكِنَّ أَكثَرَ النّاسِ لا يَعلَمونَ۝

252
00:21:33,362 --> 00:21:37,801
But most of the men know not and among these men who knows not, are the brothers of Yusuf(يوسُف).

253
00:21:40,649 --> 00:21:44,990
Yusuf(يوسُف) grew up in the house of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز).

254
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:47,839
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

255
00:21:47,869 --> 00:22:02,656
وَلَمّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُ آتَيناهُ حُكمًا وَعِلمًا ۚ

256
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:08,870
And when he, Yusuf(يوسُف) attained his full manhood, we gave him wisdom and knowledge.

257
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:11,966
Thus we reward the doers of the good.

258
00:22:12,450 --> 00:22:15,150
Hukma(حكما) and Ilmaa(علما).

259
00:22:15,848 --> 00:22:18,753
Hukum(حكم) is judgment and Ilm(علم) is knowledge?

260
00:22:19,936 --> 00:22:26,449
Why didn't Allahسُبحانه وتعالى say Hukum(حكم) only, or why didn't Allahسُبحانه وتعالى say Ilm(علم) only

261
00:22:28,623 --> 00:22:34,171
these are two different things good judgment and knowledge, and Allah gave Yusuf(يوسُف) both.

262
00:22:36,432 --> 00:22:39,567
If Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said: We have given him knowledge only.

263
00:22:41,121 --> 00:22:45,756
Knowledge could mean that you memorize a lot of Qur'an, you know, a lot of Ahadith(احاديث).

264
00:22:46,193 --> 00:22:49,342
But if you don't have a good processing of that information,

265
00:22:49,588 --> 00:22:52,620
if you don't have good judgment, you can't really do much with it.

266
00:22:52,882 --> 00:22:59,783
And we find that there are people who have a lot of knowledge with them, but they're limited in their ability to take advantage of it.

267
00:23:00,096 --> 00:23:02,424
They're limited in their ability to make use of it.

268
00:23:03,645 --> 00:23:11,360
Good judgment Hukmah(حكما) is the ability to judge events, the correct estimation and assessment of things.

269
00:23:11,661 --> 00:23:17,343
You look at something and you have wisdom in the way you assess that event and the way you analyze it

270
00:23:17,486 --> 00:23:19,639
and the way you deal with it and act upon it.

271
00:23:20,289 --> 00:23:23,303
And that is a skill and knowledge is something else.

272
00:23:23,549 --> 00:23:29,771
When you put these together, you get the perfect personality, good judgment and knowledge together.

273
00:23:30,359 --> 00:23:33,327
And that is something Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

274
00:23:33,613 --> 00:23:38,932
it is the Faham(فهم) and the understanding of the Deen(دِيْن) because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

275
00:23:38,962 --> 00:23:41,249
وربَّ حاملِ فِقهٍ إلى من هوَ أفقَهُ منهُ

276
00:23:41,507 --> 00:23:43,339
Rasool Allah ﷺ talks about;

277
00:23:43,617 --> 00:23:49,480
Maybe you are carrying Fiqh(فقه) you are delivering Fiqh(فقه) to somebody who understands this more than you.

278
00:23:51,003 --> 00:23:56,277
An example of that Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه) was sitting in his Halaqah(حلقة) in his circle

279
00:23:56,307 --> 00:24:00,854
and the way of Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه) in teaching was unique among the four Scholars;

280
00:24:01,053 --> 00:24:06,388
With Abu Hanifah رضي الله عنه he used to have a council.

281
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:09,767
So he would present an issue for debate,

282
00:24:10,259 --> 00:24:15,472
and they would discuss it and then they would give opinions and then he would make a final verdict.

283
00:24:16,266 --> 00:24:21,718
With the other three Imam(اِمَام)s, they are the ones, who would give the verdict and everybody in front of them is a student.

284
00:24:21,949 --> 00:24:24,678
When you're sitting in the Halaqah(حلقة) of Imam Malik(إمام مالك), you're a student.

285
00:24:25,154 --> 00:24:28,209
You don't argue with Imam Malik(إمام مالك) you take from him.

286
00:24:28,781 --> 00:24:30,323
With Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه), it was different.

287
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:34,802
He had, for example, Muhammed Ibn Al-Hassan(محمدإبن الحسن), and Abu Yusuf(أبويوسُف),

288
00:24:35,088 --> 00:24:38,331
we don't call them students of Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفه), we call them As-Sahiban(ألصاحبان);

289
00:24:38,490 --> 00:24:40,276
The two friends or companions.

290
00:24:40,736 --> 00:24:43,553
Even though there were students of Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفه), but we don’t call them students

291
00:24:43,736 --> 00:24:48,337
because they used to be a council with him, which he would discuss affairs with anyway.

292
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:53,536
There was one scholar of Hadith(حديث) who used to sit in this council of Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه)

293
00:24:55,176 --> 00:25:03,287
he recited the Hadith(حديث) Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه) he did not know that, that Hadith(حديث), he did not have that knowledge.

294
00:25:04,627 --> 00:25:10,365
A woman came and asked the scholar of Hadith(حديث) who was sitting in the meeting of Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفه) a question;

295
00:25:10,754 --> 00:25:12,230
she asked him a question;

296
00:25:12,570 --> 00:25:15,610
That scholar of Hadith(حديث) said; Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم), I don't know the answer.

297
00:25:17,134 --> 00:25:19,600
Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه) said: I know the answer.

298
00:25:20,267 --> 00:25:22,814
So the scholar of Hadith(حديث) said: O Imam(اِمَام) how did he know the answer?

299
00:25:22,874 --> 00:25:25,306
He said: I knew the answer from the Hadith(حديث) you just recited.

300
00:25:25,576 --> 00:25:31,152
So this is an example of somebody who's carrying the knowledge, but did not know how to implement it;

301
00:25:31,239 --> 00:25:35,430
While Imam Abu Hanifah(إمام أبوحنيفه) did not have it, but when he had it, he knew how to use it.

302
00:25:35,715 --> 00:25:43,281
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Yusuf عليه السّلام, both Hukum(حكم) and Ilm(علم) good judgment on events and knowledge.

303
00:25:44,146 --> 00:25:47,364
And this is something very important for anybody in a position of leadership.

304
00:25:47,752 --> 00:25:51,746
It's not enough to have knowledge and it's not good only to have good judgment.

305
00:25:51,806 --> 00:25:55,564
You need to have both to be an effective and successful leader.

306
00:25:56,404 --> 00:26:02,525
There is an Islamic state that happened in the North Africa a few centuries ago,

307
00:26:03,318 --> 00:26:07,474
this Islamic State was established by Ulema(علماء).

308
00:26:08,116 --> 00:26:13,507
And they implemented the Shariah(شريعة) and it was one of the honors of the Islamic history.

309
00:26:14,388 --> 00:26:20,102
When the scholars analyze the reasons of the downfall of that Islamic State,

310
00:26:20,578 --> 00:26:26,861
they say one of the reasons is because these scholars lost touch with the reality of the world around them.

311
00:26:27,461 --> 00:26:31,409
They had a lot of knowledge, but they lost touch with the reality of the world.

312
00:26:31,583 --> 00:26:36,246
They were too much busy studying the details of Fiqh(فقه) and Tafriat Al-Faqihaa(تفريات فقيهة)

313
00:26:36,357 --> 00:26:43,770
and they lost touch with the world around them and what that was one of the reasons why that state fell and was overtaken.

314
00:26:44,024 --> 00:26:48,326
Even though they were establishing Shariah(شريعة) and they were scholars, there's no doubt in their righteousness.

315
00:26:48,646 --> 00:26:51,913
Yuusuf عليه السّلام grew up in the house of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز).

316
00:26:52,271 --> 00:27:01,459
One of the Islamic scholars gives an estimate of the age of Yusuf(يوسُف), when he was adopted.

317
00:27:02,753 --> 00:27:05,245
He says he was about maybe 14 years old.

318
00:27:06,599 --> 00:27:09,937
Because Ghulam(غلام) when they have taken him from the well and they said; Ghulam(غلام);

319
00:27:10,019 --> 00:27:14,336
that is usually the age of a Ghulam(غلام), older than that is called Fatah(فتحى).

320
00:27:14,662 --> 00:27:16,754
And he says that;

321
00:27:16,865 --> 00:27:18,333
  بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُ

322
00:27:18,587 --> 00:27:23,286
would mean 25 years old, even though there's a difference in opinion on what is Balagha Ashudda(بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُ);

323
00:27:23,912 --> 00:27:29,349
we can give an estimate that the wife of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) at that time was about 40 years old.

324
00:27:30,222 --> 00:27:34,204
Because if they have adopted Yusuf(يوسُف) when he was 14,

325
00:27:34,770 --> 00:27:39,628
and let's say that she was maybe 30 years old, because her husband was already the Aziz(عزيز)

326
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:44,313
and usually to have a position of that status, you might be 40 years old.

327
00:27:44,837 --> 00:27:50,632
So by the time Yusuf(يوسُف) grows up to be 25, she might have been at that time, 40 years old.

328
00:27:51,797 --> 00:27:57,103
The wife of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) presented herself to SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف)

329
00:27:57,421 --> 00:28:01,777
and she in whose house he was sought to seduce him.

330
00:28:02,893 --> 00:28:04,547
وَغَلَّقَتِ الأَبوابَ

331
00:28:04,975 --> 00:28:06,626
And she closed the doors.

332
00:28:06,928 --> 00:28:08,658
وَقالَت هَيتَ لَكَ ۚ

333
00:28:09,150 --> 00:28:11,333
And she said: Come on you.

334
00:28:12,436 --> 00:28:17,317
She tried to sleep with him by force.

335
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:27,003
She brought him into that room, close the doors, presented herself to him and wanted to force him to commit the act of Zina(زنا).

336
00:28:27,758 --> 00:28:33,605
قالَ مَعاذَ اللَّهِ ۖ

337
00:28:34,002 --> 00:28:37,319
He said: I seek refuge in Allah.

338
00:28:37,653 --> 00:28:48,287
إِنَّهُ رَبّي أَحسَنَ مَثوايَ ۖ

339
00:28:48,716 --> 00:28:53,861
Truly your husband is my master and he made my stay agreeable.

340
00:28:54,115 --> 00:29:03,704
إِنَّهُ لا يُفلِحُ الظّالِمونَ۝

341
00:29:03,914 --> 00:29:08,455
I will never, never betray him because the wrongdoers will never be successful.

342
00:29:08,564 --> 00:29:09,519
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

343
00:29:10,353 --> 00:29:11,599
قالَ مَعاذَ اللَّهِ ۖ

344
00:29:12,092 --> 00:29:14,044
I seek refuge in Allah.

345
00:29:15,329 --> 00:29:25,124
So first of all, look at this, first of all, he's not stopping her, in his confidence in his own self.

346
00:29:25,973 --> 00:29:30,965
He's asking Allah to help him, Maadh Allah(معاذ); I seek refuge in Allah; O Allah help me.

347
00:29:31,167 --> 00:29:32,121
And then he said;

348
00:29:32,209 --> 00:29:33,996
إِنَّهُ رَبّي أَحسَنَ مَثوايَ ۖ

349
00:29:34,232 --> 00:29:39,638
Your husband is my master, and he has been very well with me; he has treated me very well.

350
00:29:40,174 --> 00:29:42,659
Look at the gratitude that SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) had,

351
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:47,717
even though he was a slave, and this was a slave master, he did not have any hatred against him.

352
00:29:48,106 --> 00:29:55,141
In fact, he viewed him as somebody who needs to be respected because he dealt with him in a very good and respectable way.

353
00:29:55,776 --> 00:29:56,364
And then he said;

354
00:29:56,394 --> 00:29:57,952
إِنَّهُ لا يُفلِحُ الظّالِمونَ۝

355
00:29:57,976 --> 00:30:01,681
The ones, who betray and the ones who do wrong; they can never be successful.

356
00:30:02,387 --> 00:30:03,591
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

357
00:30:03,621 --> 00:30:08,158
وَلَقَد هَمَّت بِهِ ۖ

358
00:30:09,515 --> 00:30:20,510
