541
00:46:49,826 --> 00:46:52,890
At least I will be away from this Fitnah(فِتْنَه); it's better for me.

542
00:46:53,707 --> 00:47:02,897
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Yusuf(يوسُف) is doing all of this to keep away from one of the most powerful seducing things that could affect a man.

543
00:47:04,476 --> 00:47:14,253
Not only is it the beauty and the and the lust and the encouragement of the woman and the society and the environment that Yusuf(يوسُف) is living in,

544
00:47:14,283 --> 00:47:17,698
but he's also being coerced and forced to commit Zina(زنا).

545
00:47:18,420 --> 00:47:19,841
Yusuf(يوسُف) said: O Allah take me to jail

546
00:47:19,950 --> 00:47:24,894
 going to jail is better for me than responding to what they want me to do.

547
00:47:25,561 --> 00:47:26,330
And then he said;

548
00:47:26,648 --> 00:47:46,154
وَإِلّا تَصرِف عَنّي كَيدَهُنَّ أَصبُ إِلَيهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِنَ الجاهِلينَ۝

549
00:47:46,578 --> 00:47:49,535
Unless You turn away their plot from me,

550
00:47:49,829 --> 00:47:57,937
I will feel inclined towards them and be one of those who commit the sin and one of those who are ignorant.

551
00:47:58,334 --> 00:48:03,364
He said: O Allah, if you do not take away this from me, I am weak;

552
00:48:03,992 --> 00:48:06,262
I am weak and I'm going to fall into this.

553
00:48:06,801 --> 00:48:10,462
An admission from SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف) of his weakness, we are weak.

554
00:48:11,470 --> 00:48:13,153
We should never think that we're strong.

555
00:48:13,558 --> 00:48:15,931
Our strength comes from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

556
00:48:16,410 --> 00:48:24,526
and this is the Dua(دُعَا) that we should say, in environments like this, which are similar to the environment of Yusuf عليه السّلام.

557
00:48:25,407 --> 00:48:29,979
وَإِلّا تَصرِف عَنّي كَيدَهُنَّ أَصبُ إِلَيهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِنَ الجاهِلينَ۝

558
00:48:30,249 --> 00:48:38,608
O Allah unless you turn away their plot from me; I will feel inclined towards them and be one of the ignorance.

559
00:48:39,330 --> 00:48:50,809
فَاستَجابَ لَهُ رَبُّهُ فَصَرَفَ عَنهُ كَيدَهُنَّ ۚ

560
00:48:52,999 --> 00:49:02,093
إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّميعُ العَليمُ۝

561
00:49:02,414 --> 00:49:07,443
So his Lord answered his invocation and turn away from him, their plot.

562
00:49:07,563 --> 00:49:10,571
Verily He is the All Hearer and the All Knower.

563
00:49:11,221 --> 00:49:31,396
ثُمَّ بَدا لَهُم مِن بَعدِ ما رَأَوُا الآياتِ لَيَسجُنُنَّهُ حَتّىٰ حينٍ۝

564
00:49:31,618 --> 00:49:37,391
Then it appeared to them after they had seen the proofs of his innocence to imprison him for a time.

565
00:49:38,025 --> 00:49:41,240
Now the news is spread; it's a scandal now.

566
00:49:41,779 --> 00:49:46,464
How can they solve the problem by taking the innocent to jail.

567
00:49:47,893 --> 00:49:56,249
Instead of stopping, the wife of Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) they took the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah Yusuf(يوسُف) and they put him in jail.

568
00:49:57,805 --> 00:50:01,416
He was oppressed, and put in jail even though he was innocent.

569
00:50:03,408 --> 00:50:06,913
There were two men who were with him in jail.

570
00:50:09,397 --> 00:50:11,317
And these two men saw a dream;

571
00:50:14,015 --> 00:50:21,095
one of them saw a dream in which he is pressing wine

572
00:50:23,270 --> 00:50:30,352
and the other one saw a dream in which he is carrying on his head some bread

573
00:50:31,312 --> 00:50:35,651
and there are some birds who are eating from that bread.

574
00:50:36,064 --> 00:50:56,717
وَدَخَلَ مَعَهُ السِّجنَ فَتَيانِ ۖ قالَ أَحَدُهُما إِنّي أَراني أَعصِرُ خَمرًا ۖ

575
00:50:59,654 --> 00:51:25,952
وَقالَ الآخَرُ إِنّي أَراني أَحمِلُ فَوقَ رَأسي خُبزًا تَأكُلُ الطَّيرُ مِنهُ ۖ نَبِّئنا بِتَأويلِهِ ۖ

576
00:51:29,014 --> 00:51:38,083
إِنّا نَراكَ مِنَ المُحسِنينَ۝

577
00:51:38,429 --> 00:51:43,614
They said: Because we see that you are of those, who are righteous.

578
00:51:44,050 --> 00:51:48,455
We want you to tell us the interpretation of this dream.

579
00:51:49,558 --> 00:51:53,789
Yusuf عليه السّلام told them;

580
00:51:54,360 --> 00:52:01,120
No food will come to you, but I will inform you it's interpretation before it comes.

581
00:52:01,993 --> 00:52:28,589
قالَ لا يَأتيكُما طَعامٌ تُرزَقانِهِ إِلّا نَبَّأتُكُما بِتَأويلِهِ قَبلَ أَن يَأتِيَكُما ۚ

582
00:52:29,232 --> 00:52:32,399
The Mufassireen(مفسرين) have different opinions about this one of them is that

583
00:52:32,597 --> 00:52:38,790
Sayidina Yusuf عليه السّلام told them I will tell you the interpretation of the dream before your next meal is served.

584
00:52:40,250 --> 00:52:43,437
Before your next meal is served, you will have the interpretation of the dream.

585
00:52:46,680 --> 00:52:52,630
And then notice the personality of the Daiyah(داعية), the preacher to Islam.

586
00:52:53,305 --> 00:52:57,805
They asked him a question about an interpretation of a dream.

587
00:52:59,336 --> 00:53:00,117
He said;

588
00:53:00,379 --> 00:53:02,562
ذٰلِكُما مِمّا عَلَّمَني رَبّي ۚ

589
00:53:03,022 --> 00:53:04,302
Now this is number two.

590
00:53:04,332 --> 00:53:05,165
Number one;

591
00:53:05,474 --> 00:53:06,173
He told them.

592
00:53:06,203 --> 00:53:07,893
طَعامٌ تُرزَقانِهِ

593
00:53:09,021 --> 00:53:12,125
Before you receive your next meal, but he said;

594
00:53:12,315 --> 00:53:13,394
Turzaqanihi(ترزقانه)

595
00:53:13,855 --> 00:53:15,264
it is Rizq(رزق) from Allah.

596
00:53:16,053 --> 00:53:17,827
So he's driving some concepts to them.

597
00:53:17,874 --> 00:53:22,144
So number one is telling them that this food that you will receive is from Allah.

598
00:53:23,255 --> 00:53:32,644
ذٰلِكُما مِمّا عَلَّمَني رَبّي ۚ

599
00:53:33,816 --> 00:53:36,996
That is of the knowledge that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has taught me.

600
00:53:37,026 --> 00:53:41,860
Meaning I'm not gonna tell you the interpretation of the dream from my own knowledge and skills.

601
00:53:41,890 --> 00:53:44,169
This is knowledge that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has taught me.

602
00:53:44,550 --> 00:53:46,693
So he's giving credit to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

603
00:53:48,029 --> 00:53:49,013
Number three;

604
00:53:49,640 --> 00:54:11,830
إِنّي تَرَكتُ مِلَّةَ قَومٍ لا يُؤمِنونَ بِاللَّهِ وَهُم بِالآخِرَةِ هُم كافِرونَ۝

605
00:54:12,414 --> 00:54:17,906
I have abandoned the religion of a people that believe not in Allah.

606
00:54:18,192 --> 00:54:20,482
Now what does this have to do with interpretation of the dreams?

607
00:54:20,720 --> 00:54:23,878
This is pure Da'wah(دعوة), that he is delivering to these people.

608
00:54:23,908 --> 00:54:27,760
He said: I have left the religion of the people, who disbelieve in Allah.

609
00:54:28,536 --> 00:54:31,417
He is talking about the religion that they're following.

610
00:54:32,005 --> 00:54:33,973
He said: I have abandoned that religion,

611
00:54:34,163 --> 00:54:36,477
وَهُم بِالآخِرَةِ هُم كافِرونَ۝

612
00:54:36,640 --> 00:54:39,332
And they disbelieve in the Akhirah(آخرة).

613
00:54:40,245 --> 00:54:44,861
So he is establishing in them the belief in Allah and the belief in Akhirah(آخرة)

614
00:54:44,925 --> 00:54:51,260
because there is no religion that was revealed to Nabi(نَبِي), except that it has in it; a pillar of faith, which is Akhirah(آخرة).

615
00:54:52,387 --> 00:54:54,514
And then number five, he said;

616
00:54:54,768 --> 00:55:13,874
وَاتَّبَعتُ مِلَّةَ آبائي إِبراهيمَ وَإِسحاقَ وَيَعقوبَ ۚ

617
00:55:14,572 --> 00:55:20,970
And I followed the religion of my father's Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), Is'haq(إسحاق) and Yaqoob(يعقوب).

618
00:55:21,343 --> 00:55:24,185
Why did he tell them that I followed the religion of my fathers.

619
00:55:25,145 --> 00:55:31,376
Ibrahim عليه السّلام was the caller of truth of Tawheed(توحيد) in that time.

620
00:55:32,503 --> 00:55:33,733
He was the believer.

621
00:55:35,439 --> 00:55:41,786
And the belief in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was among his children, it wasn't widespread.

622
00:55:43,064 --> 00:55:48,481
So the family of Ibrahim عليه السّلام were famous that they were the families of Islam.

623
00:55:51,052 --> 00:55:58,997
The people in Egypt have heard about the news of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and this Is'haq(إسحاق) and Yaqoob(يعقوب) and the religion of Tawheed(توحيد).

624
00:55:59,552 --> 00:56:03,891
So Yusuf(يوسُف) is telling them about it; He's telling them this is the religion that I follow.

625
00:56:05,391 --> 00:56:10,309
So he's telling them: I'm following the religion of my father's Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Is'haq(إسحاق) and Yaqoob(يعقوب)

626
00:56:10,594 --> 00:56:13,221
because they were the representations after Tawheed(توحيد).

627
00:56:13,396 --> 00:56:16,658
They were the representations of the oneness of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى .

628
00:56:16,689 --> 00:56:19,673
It was among this blessed family of Ibrahim عليه السلام.

629
00:56:20,507 --> 00:56:21,455
Number six;

630
00:56:21,789 --> 00:56:35,057
ما كانَ لَنا أَن نُشرِكَ بِاللَّهِ مِن شَيءٍ

631
00:56:35,844 --> 00:56:40,138
And never could we attribute any partners whatsoever to Allah.

632
00:56:41,297 --> 00:56:46,119
The people in Egypt at that time knew the concept of Allah but they knew it in a form of Shirk(شرك);

633
00:56:46,389 --> 00:56:50,040
because we'll find throughout the story of Yusuf(يوسُف) that they knew about Allah;

634
00:56:50,238 --> 00:56:53,100
because we talked about Al-Aziz(ألعزيز) is telling his wife;

635
00:56:53,130 --> 00:56:54,144
 فاستغفري لذنبك

636
00:56:54,429 --> 00:56:56,096
Ask Allah to forgive your sin.

637
00:56:56,294 --> 00:57:02,822
So they knew about Allahسُبحانه وتعالى but they were attributing, other gods with him like the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

638
00:57:03,024 --> 00:57:04,733
they knew about Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

639
00:57:04,778 --> 00:57:08,612
But they used to believe in other idols and gods and then he said;

640
00:57:08,707 --> 00:57:32,329
ذٰلِكَ مِن فَضلِ اللَّهِ عَلَينا وَعَلَى النّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ أَكثَرَ النّاسِ لا يَشكُرونَ۝

641
00:57:33,091 --> 00:57:33,972
Number seven;

642
00:57:34,186 --> 00:57:38,249
this is from the grace of Allah to us and to mankind.

643
00:57:38,653 --> 00:57:40,947
وَلٰكِنَّ أَكثَرَ النّاسِ لا يَشكُرونَ۝

644
00:57:41,294 --> 00:57:43,881
But most of mankind do not thank.

645
00:57:44,415 --> 00:57:50,722
Yusuf(يوسُف) is saying that this message of Tawheed(توحيد) is a blessing of Allah on us and it's a blessing of Allah on all mankind.

646
00:57:51,531 --> 00:57:56,456
Because the Ibrahim عليه السّلام was calling everyone to Islam, so it's a blessing on everyone.

647
00:57:57,906 --> 00:58:00,273
The religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is a blessing for everyone.

648
00:58:01,232 --> 00:58:04,580
This is an introduction and then he came to interpret the dream.

649
00:58:05,229 --> 00:58:08,057
But he gave them another introduction before he interpreted the dream.

650
00:58:08,678 --> 00:58:12,374
They asked him a straight question; Tell us the interpretation of this dream.

651
00:58:12,664 --> 00:58:13,586
What was his answer?

652
00:58:13,695 --> 00:58:14,284
He said;

653
00:58:14,539 --> 00:58:16,112
يا صاحِبَيِ السِّجنِ

654
00:58:16,689 --> 00:58:20,149
O companions of the prison and look at the choice of words.

655
00:58:20,209 --> 00:58:21,429
يا صاحِبَيِ السِّجنِ

656
00:58:21,674 --> 00:58:24,596
O companions; he's taking them as companions and friends.

657
00:58:25,137 --> 00:58:29,375
He is having a social relation with them some closeness?

658
00:58:29,462 --> 00:58:30,659
يا صاحِبَيِ السِّجنِ

659
00:58:31,042 --> 00:58:35,770
A very soft way of speaking to them; O companions of jail, you're my companions.

660
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:38,628
And then he sends a question to them;

661
00:58:39,104 --> 00:59:01,182
يا صاحِبَيِ السِّجنِ أَأَربابٌ مُتَفَرِّقونَ خَيرٌ أَمِ اللَّهُ الواحِدُ القَهّارُ۝

662
00:59:01,636 --> 00:59:06,768
Are many different gods better or Allah, the One that irresistible?

663
00:59:07,734 --> 00:59:14,657
He's not telling them straightly Allah is better; He's asking them a question; to make them use their mind.

664
00:59:15,025 --> 00:59:17,925
It is obvious because why is he asking this particular question?

665
00:59:18,185 --> 00:59:24,563
Because it is obvious to the human intellect and the human mind and the human heart, that there's only one God.

666
00:59:25,068 --> 00:59:26,624
Allah is Al-Qahhaar(ألقهار)

667
00:59:27,093 --> 00:59:31,436
Al-Qahhaar(ألقهار) means He is the one, who is overwhelming and dominant over everything.

668
00:59:32,309 --> 00:59:37,704
So all of these other gods that you are establishing, besides Allah, they have no power whatsoever.

669
00:59:38,497 --> 00:59:39,818
So he ask them this question.

670
00:59:40,842 --> 00:59:42,321
And then he's giving them the answer.

671
00:59:42,631 --> 00:59:44,791
He gave them the question so that they would think,

672
00:59:45,203 --> 00:59:49,243
and he's preparing them to receive the next piece of information that he will give them.

673
00:59:49,560 --> 00:59:50,567
He told them;

674
00:59:50,671 --> 01:00:17,074
ما تَعبُدونَ مِن دونِهِ إِلّا أَسماءً سَمَّيتُموها أَنتُم وَآباؤُكُم

675
01:00:19,354 --> 01:00:43,481
سَمَّيتُموها أَنتُم وَآباؤُكُم ما أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ بِها مِن سُلطانٍ ۚ

676
01:00:43,782 --> 01:00:52,827
You do not worship besides Him but only names which you have forged - you and your father's for which Allah has sent down no authority.

677
01:00:53,187 --> 01:00:56,132
Asmaa(أسماء) names, what is the name?

678
01:00:56,905 --> 01:01:08,413
A name is an abstract thing, the name itself has no value, the substance which are naming that has the value.

679
01:01:08,623 --> 01:01:11,825
Yusuf(يوسُف) is telling them that these gods have no substance, they don't even exist.

680
01:01:11,898 --> 01:01:16,133
There's nothing behind it; it's just a name; it's just a label; there's nothing behind it.

681
01:01:16,400 --> 01:01:17,708
أَسماءً سَمَّيتُموها

682
01:01:17,951 --> 01:01:21,732
These are names you forged with your father's before.

683
01:01:22,040 --> 01:01:23,576
ما أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ بِها مِن سُلطانٍ ۚ

684
01:01:23,786 --> 01:01:26,501
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not instruct or commanded us to do this.

685
01:01:27,951 --> 01:01:28,611
Then he said;

686
01:01:28,716 --> 01:01:36,756
إِنِ الحُكمُ إِلّا لِلَّهِ ۚ

687
01:01:37,204 --> 01:01:40,173
The command is for none but Allah;

688
01:01:40,440 --> 01:01:48,703
Al-Hukm(ألحكم); the governance and the rule and the command belongs to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in all of our affairs in everything,

689
01:01:49,699 --> 01:01:56,553
we need to realize that we are following an incomplete form of Islam today.

690
01:01:58,639 --> 01:02:01,946
We're following the brand of Islam that is missing the Shariah(شريعة).

691
01:02:02,754 --> 01:02:04,053
The Shariah(شريعة) is left out.

692
01:02:04,529 --> 01:02:09,859
We are following a certain aspect of Islam which is the daily rituals of Ibadah(عبادة)

693
01:02:10,205 --> 01:02:16,294
and some things that we do in the Masjid(مسجد) and some very little Akhlaq(أخلاق) that we have and that's it.

694
01:02:16,640 --> 01:02:19,690
 But we're missing the Shariah(شريعة); the law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

695
01:02:19,762 --> 01:02:26,000
we're missing the important Akhlaq(أخلاق), we're missing the way of dealing in business, we're missing all of this.

696
01:02:26,764 --> 01:02:33,058
And if we do not have the intention to bring it back, and if we do not strive and struggle to do so,

697
01:02:33,331 --> 01:02:36,745
then we are guilty of following an incomplete form of Islam.

698
01:02:37,849 --> 01:02:41,404
And the only excuse we would have in front of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is;

699
01:02:41,627 --> 01:02:46,000
if we strive and struggle to bring back the complete form of Islam.

700
01:02:46,137 --> 01:02:50,725
If we do that, then we hope that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will forgive us for this shortcoming.

701
01:02:50,884 --> 01:02:51,621
Yusuf(يوسُف) is saying;

702
01:02:51,651 --> 01:02:52,897
إِنِ الحُكمُ إِلّا لِلَّهِ ۚ

703
01:02:52,927 --> 01:02:54,670
All Command belongs to Allah.

704
01:02:55,167 --> 01:02:57,245
Do we follow the commandments of Allah in business?

705
01:02:57,649 --> 01:03:00,267
Do we follow the commandments of Allah in criminal law.?

706
01:03:00,485 --> 01:03:03,255
Do we follow the commandments of Allah in international law?

707
01:03:03,436 --> 01:03:05,680
Do you follow the commandments of Allah in politics?

708
01:03:05,889 --> 01:03:07,977
Do you follow the commandments of Allah in economics?

709
01:03:08,251 --> 01:03:11,029
Do you follow the commandments of Allah in social laws?

710
01:03:12,125 --> 01:03:14,687
If we are leaving all of this out, what are we following?

711
01:03:15,622 --> 01:03:20,294
And then Yusuf(يوسُف) is telling them, the justification, why the rules should belong to Allah

712
01:03:20,324 --> 01:03:21,195
because he says;

713
01:03:21,604 --> 01:03:34,142
أَمَرَ أَلّا تَعبُدوا إِلّا إِيّاهُ ۚ

714
01:03:34,640 --> 01:03:38,480
He has ordered you to worship none but Him; so this is part of worship.

715
01:03:39,420 --> 01:03:43,835
The reason why, Hukum(حكم) should belong to Allah; is because it is part of worship.

716
01:03:44,261 --> 01:03:50,492
And if we are not worshiping Allah in the laws of social life and politics and economics,

717
01:03:50,651 --> 01:03:53,675
that means we are taking other gods besides Allah.

718
01:03:54,559 --> 01:03:57,178
And that's why when Odae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) walked in;

719
01:03:57,359 --> 01:03:59,891
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a cross hanging on his chest?

720
01:04:00,750 --> 01:04:01,739
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

721
01:04:01,769 --> 01:04:05,058
اتَّخَذُوا أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ أَرْبَابًا من دون الله

722
01:04:05,267 --> 01:04:09,562
They have taken their priests and the rabbi's Gods besides Allah.

723
01:04:09,995 --> 01:04:12,578
Odae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) said: No; We do not worship our priests.

724
01:04:12,852 --> 01:04:15,096
He was a Christian who had the cross hanging on his chest.

725
01:04:15,363 --> 01:04:20,616
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Didn't your priests make the Halal(حلال); Haram(حرام) and the Haram(حرام); Halal(حلال)?

726
01:04:20,958 --> 01:04:23,252
He said: Yes! He said that is worshipping them.

727
01:04:24,436 --> 01:04:29,558
If you give a human being the authority to say that the Halal(حلال) is Haram(حرام) and the Haram(حرام) is Halal(حلال),

728
01:04:29,710 --> 01:04:32,192
you have taken him as a god besides Allah.

729
01:04:32,964 --> 01:04:36,210
And that is what we have done in a lot of aspects of our life.

730
01:04:36,260 --> 01:04:43,579
Actually the major portion of our life, we have given the authority to man and we have taken it from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

731
01:04:45,405 --> 01:04:46,250
So Yusuf(يوسُف) is telling them;

732
01:04:46,280 --> 01:04:49,259
إِنِ الحُكمُ إِلّا لِلَّهِ ۚ أَمَرَ أَلّا تَعبُدوا إِلّا إِيّاهُ ۚ

733
01:04:49,319 --> 01:04:53,826
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى the commandment belongs to Him and Allah has instructed you to worship none but Him.

734
01:04:54,049 --> 01:05:11,396
ذٰلِكَ الدّينُ القَيِّمُ وَلٰكِنَّ أَكثَرَ النّاسِ لا يَعلَمونَ۝

735
01:05:11,958 --> 01:05:18,105
That is the true religion; If you want the true religion that is the true religion.

736
01:05:18,913 --> 01:05:20,556
وَلٰكِنَّ أَكثَرَ النّاسِ لا يَعلَمونَ۝

737
01:05:20,796 --> 01:05:22,833
But most men know not.

738
01:05:26,216 --> 01:05:28,773
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

